From 219c4b70a755fd1c687021ad031cff2a3fd06e85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:38:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][Network] Projector control: picture modes of their
 own for the menus and SDR in BT.2020

An owner of a JVC NZ800 who maps HDR to SDR in BT.2020 asked for one
picture mode for the menus (a user mode in Rec.709 or DCI) and another
for the videos (a user mode in BT.2020): the control chose the mode by
the signal that goes out, and the menus and SDR video were both SDR,
so they shared one mode.

The kind of an SDR signal is now refined (KindOf(), ProjectorPolicy.h):
the menus while no video plays (a video paused with its controls shown
still plays: IsPlayingVideo()), SDR in BT.2020 while the video's SDR
picture goes out in BT.2020 (an SDR video of BT.2020 kept in it, or HDR
mapped to SDR in BT.2020), SDR in DCI-P3 while HDR is mapped to SDR in
it; each with its own setting, "As for SDR video" by default. A kind
left at that default is SDR itself, so the control does exactly what it
did before for anyone who does not set one: no mode is sent when a
video ends, nor when one starts in SDR. The kind is followed as every
kind is: taken once it has lasted SIGNAL_SECONDS, so the next video of
a playlist does not send the mode of the menus in between, and each
kind once.

The gamut is the renderer's own (CBaseRenderer::SdrGamutOut():
CLinuxRendererGLES says the container it drew the SDR picture into,
SdrWideConfigure()), fed to the control at each picture presented while
the control is on (FeedGamut(), a store under the lock of the feed), and
taken as BT.709 where it was not told in the last two seconds. Nothing
of the window system changes.

The label of the mode for SDR now says "SDR video", and its help no
longer says that the menus are SDR. English, and the three Spanish
languages of Estuary.
